#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501158 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124603 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7f1e542-f0a2-54ea-ba7f-0a9928415907" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Using the Definition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "394529b7-5240-5ff7-90db-e1add45b32a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500582} {:answer/id #uuid "825811a4-08b5-5ffb-990f-7e501d2498b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500736} {:answer/id #uuid "9efa7096-ec71-5ba8-a546-d69b56f674bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500789} {:answer/id #uuid "aad3aeef-b512-5754-9b36-a0105a67e7d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500820} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f6fe27-6dff-5e8f-81fc-28e28ad0e3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "825811a4-08b5-5ffb-990f-7e501d2498b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500736} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b795f03-1c4c-51ce-9ec3-51380c3631d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501074}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a497a8c-181f-5ddb-8e0c-d7f0dcc66829" :question/math-academy-id "q-38861" :question/problem "Suppose $T:V\\to W$ is a linear map and $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ are the bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W$, respectively. Find the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T$ relative to these bases, if \n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})=-3{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2},\\,$ $T({b}_{2})={c}_{1}-4{c}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{3})=5{c}_{1}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the images of vectors in $B$ relative to the basis $C:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1})=-3{c}_{1}-5{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{1})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{2})={c}_{1}-4{c}_{2} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T({b}_{3})=5{c}_{1} & \\,⟹\\,[T({b}_{3})]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1}),$ $T({b}_{2})$ and $T({b}_{3})$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501135 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124604 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0587fad6-5ef2-5200-9b60-ddbd0bc21ba7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Map Relative to Two Bases Given One Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3811dc15-f044-5933-86e0-b81332887411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500581} {:answer/id #uuid "575b1543-5913-5111-9e9c-4cf207869497" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500645} {:answer/id #uuid "5e277c6c-dcd2-5491-b1f3-c7fa6def4dfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500660} {:answer/id #uuid "6a9c8e6c-8875-5f05-83c5-ba640b983ce5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500687} {:answer/id #uuid "be36abcb-60b4-5b59-8d60-819c63d7b780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be36abcb-60b4-5b59-8d60-819c63d7b780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500862} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4374709-dd94-564d-a093-c34e0f6d470b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501125}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00e54e6a-cd0f-51b4-97b3-2489c07dd2c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-97574" :question/problem "Consider the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ of the vector space $V$ and the basis $C$ of ${R}^{2}$ given by\n\n$$\nC=\\{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\}.\n$$\n\nFind the matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the map $T:V\\to {R}^{2}$ relative to these bases if \n\n$$\nT({b}_{1})=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,T({b}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $[T]_{B|C}$ is the matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nFirst, we need to find the coordinates of $T({b}_{i})$ relative to the basis $C$ for each $i=1,2.$ We can do this simultaneously by considering the following matrix:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 9 & -3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-\\frac{1}{3}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the right-hand side gives the matrix of the linear transformation relative to the bases $B$ and $C:$\n\n$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124542 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b4984b8-1073-51f4-bbe6-0c45bb082a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500491} {:answer/id #uuid "1601e7df-ddae-5494-a41c-da35e76fa3c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500516} {:answer/id #uuid "83748e6b-9023-5628-b878-282bfb4de93b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500739} {:answer/id #uuid "97e4106e-ea27-5370-8a2c-fa0b2b2c526d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500777} {:answer/id #uuid "9d7cb8ed-bc84-5b04-a0d8-47c0b7dd5e6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b4984b8-1073-51f4-bbe6-0c45bb082a34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500491} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b8b066b-e90d-5c38-b2a6-4d8b3185f0d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba29e43e-8fe2-5bbe-a64e-366d83a4fca9" :question/math-academy-id "q-97578" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 7 \\\\ 6 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124542 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84947238-f446-5261-8ecd-ee263f64e04f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Under a Linear Map Given the Matrix Relative to Two Bases"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4176c859-5854-5080-bf2e-b0f94f0b8361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361127} {:answer/id #uuid "6cb06e3c-e23d-5e91-bbec-4e481c417779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361321} {:answer/id #uuid "7eaadcc6-81a8-5407-bdd2-2c06f604c335" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361396} {:answer/id #uuid "a69c20d3-4c5a-587d-8103-f2c720627c8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361584} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ce3e71-5c81-5e9f-a3e1-5fabb47b6eec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8ce3e71-5c81-5e9f-a3e1-5fabb47b6eec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361801} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eea433c-814e-5e0e-919d-f13b06399a26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c64bcdb5-768e-5293-a151-ad4d8fbb8250" :question/math-academy-id "q-97579" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}9 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSuppose $B$ and $C$ are bases of the vector spaces $V$ and $W,$ respectively. The matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:V\\to W$ relative to these bases, and the coordinates of the vector $x\\in V$ relative to $B$ are shown above. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "The coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124543 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8725caed-481c-5fbe-a0c4-cffdcb308881" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Vector Given With Respect to the Standard Basis Under a Linear Map"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "336fb41f-4416-5b90-9963-63b715d894cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361063} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7b5d9e-e2af-5819-9157-eb95f22a5fe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361315} {:answer/id #uuid "860742e3-e187-5777-a59d-99f7335da169" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361436} {:answer/id #uuid "d4184a13-5037-5335-bef6-cc89b6e2f44f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361788} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c815cc-4d5f-5de4-92b1-bdce9f7a0197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7c815cc-4d5f-5de4-92b1-bdce9f7a0197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361873} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e0a7bfb-89f3-51f0-b3f7-efaec681dd46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362037}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29ca0842-b657-584e-9ec2-fc1fbb7af353" :question/math-academy-id "q-97584" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\},\\,[T]_{B|C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ (shown above) and a basis $C$ of ${R}^{3}.$\nThe matrix $[T]_{B|C}$ of the linear map $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3}$ relative to these bases, and the vector $x\\in {R}^{2},$ are also given. Find $[T(x)]_{C}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the coordinates of the image of $x$ under $T$ relative to the basis $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to find $[x]_{B},$ the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B.$ So, let\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives us the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}=-4 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now row-reduce the corresponding augmented matrix using Gaussian elimination, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{C} & =[T]_{B|C}\\cdot [x]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
